/* Layout for the new-character preview frame (P5: character_preview_window).
   Palette/border come from theme.rcss (linked first in character_preview.rml);
   this file owns only the box's own layout. Lengths in dp.

   A single absolutely-positioned bordered box whose centre is transparent so the
   GPU character sprite shows through (the box only replaces the curses draw_border
   chrome). C++ sets #cp-box left/top/width/height each redraw from the preview
   rect. A centred "CHARACTER PREVIEW" title strip sits at the top edge with an
   opaque background so it stays legible over the sprite; the rest of the box has
   no fill. */

/* The missions gotcha (see newcharpoints.rcss:2): an unsized body SHRINK-WRAPS,
   so #cp-box's containing block collapses to the title text and the left/top/
   width/height percentages C++ sets each redraw all resolve against ~0. The box
   then strands itself at the screen's top-left while the avatar sprite draws at
   the correct rect, which is exactly how this looked before. */
body {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
}
.cp-box {
    position: absolute;
    border: 1dp {{bg4}};
    /* no background-color: the centre stays transparent for the sprite */
}

.cp-title {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    background-color: {{bg}};
    color: {{fg}};
    padding: 0 2dp;
}
